    {
        "user": "U58JZC631",
        "type": "message",
        "ts": "1715895823.824389",
        "client_msg_id": "9ec561f0-54ad-4528-82ee-327e9ce97256",
        "text": "_Without treatment, mental health conditions worsen and can lead to a crisis, resulting in unemployment, homelessness or incarceration._ \n\n_In 2023, city dispatchers in San Francisco received 23,000 calls about people having a crisis or attempting suicide, Madison Alvarado and Yesica Prado of the San Francisco Public Press found. In investigating the city’s response system, they learned San Francisco spends millions of tax dollars annually on a myriad of crisis services in the city. Yet while people may be held and treated for emergency care, they are often released with no long-term treatment plan, leading to a cyclical pattern._",
        "team": "T036YAYMK",
        "user_team": "T036YAYMK",
        "source_team": "T036YAYMK",
        "user_profile": {
            "avatar_hash": "8aa29efb4a30",
            "image_72": "https:\/\/avatars.slack-edge.com\/2024-02-13\/6619261340375_8aa29efb4a303e3101dd_72.jpg",
            "first_name": "Noah",
            "real_name": "Noah Arroyo",
            "display_name": "noah",
            "team": "T036YAYMK",
            "name": "noah",
            "is_restricted": false,
            "is_ultra_restricted": false
        },
        "blocks": [
            {
                "type": "rich_text",
                "block_id": "KeKwL",
                "elements": [
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_section",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "Without treatment, mental health conditions worsen and can lead to a crisis, resulting in unemployment, homelessness or incarceration. \n",
                                "style": {
                                    "italic": true
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "\n"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "In 2023, city dispatchers in San Francisco received 23,000 calls about people having a crisis or attempting suicide, Madison Alvarado and Yesica Prado of the San Francisco Public Press found. In investigating the city’s response system, they learned San Francisco spends millions of tax dollars annually on a myriad of crisis services in the city. Yet while people may be held and treated for emergency care, they are often released with no long-term treatment plan, leading to a cyclical pattern.",
                                "style": {
                                    "italic": true
                                }
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            }
        ]
    },
